  "content_description": "",
  "content_text_body": "Instead of creating another meeting or action step to share information from other parts of the business, look for work that is already underway in different departments.\n\n[Making Collaboration a Habit](video \"LiL3_Collaboration_Habit\")\n\n**Watch**: *Making Collaboration a Habit*\n\n---\n\n* Some groups already have weekly or monthly newsletters. Ask to be added to the distribution list and scan the headlines for information that is relevant to your team.\n\n* Look for recurring Town Hall or team meetings that a member of your team can audit and report back key takeaways.\n\n* Encourage your team to invite cross-functional partners in their own planning meetings where an outside perspective would be valuable.\n\n* If you see an example of a missed opportunity due to poor cross-functional communication, diagnose where the miss was and how you can better communicate in advance before it becomes a bigger problem.\n\n* Have senior leaders encourage and reward \"intrapreneurial\u00e2\u20ac\u009d behavior when departments and teams adapt ideas/approaches/tools from other areas of the business and use them in a new way.",
